---
import Blurb from '../../Blurb.astro';
import './SpecialiseSection.css';

// Note: ADD A FRAMEWORKS SECTION HERE!
const languages = [
  {
    name: 'JavaScript/TypeScript',
    reason: 'An absolute weapon in the browser, JS is a critical tool to have in one\'s toolkit, from vanilla JS for simple but elegant solutions to react.js for sophisticated UI, JavaScript has the power to knock the user\'s socks off!',
    logos: [
      { label: 'JS', bg: '#F7DF1E', fg: '#1a1a1a' },
      { label: 'TS', bg: '#3178C6', fg: '#ffffff' },
    ],
  },
  {
    name: 'Python',
    reason: 'From serverless firebase/AWS functions, basic API test scripts to working with data and AI, python has proven itself time and time again to be a robust and flexible language allowing for untapped levels of creativity. It is one of my dearest.',
    logos: [{ label: 'Py', bg: '#4B8B3B', fg: '#ffffff' }],
  },
  {
    name: 'CSharp',
    reason: 'CSharp and by extension dotnet, is an heavy hitter in writing backend solutions, this strongly typed but succinct language brings sophisticated backend solutions to life, and who doesn\'t love that!',
    logos: [{ label: 'C#', bg: '#684DBA', fg: '#ffffff' }, { label: 'Dotnet', bg: '#684DBA', fg: '#ffffff' }],
  },
  {
    name: 'Dart',
    reason: 'A relative newcomer to my list, dart (and flutter) has made mobile app development the easiest it has ever been, it\'s purpose built and just makes sense, when starting a mobile app, I would not choose anything else.',
    logos: [{ label: 'Dart', bg: '#0175C2', fg: '#ffffff' }, { label: 'Flutter', bg: '#0175C2', fg: '#ffffff' }],
  },
];
---

<Blurb id="craft" align="left" title="What do I specialise in?">
  <p>
    I consider 4 languages to be my specialty, these 4 are very close to my heart as they have
    served me well over the years.
  </p>
  <div class="language-list">
    {languages.map((lang) => (
      <div class="language-item">
        <h3>{lang.name}</h3>
        <p>{lang.reason}</p>
        <div class="language-logos">
          {lang.logos.map((logo) => (
            <span class="language-logo" style={`background:${logo.bg}; color:${logo.fg};`}>
              {logo.label}
            </span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</Blurb>
